    description: "## What\nBuild a Y.Doc (pycrdt) from the compiled tracker state and keep it current as ops land, per the shape decided in the live-document ADR (item A of this set). Read side only; no writes back to the tracker.\n## How\n- Reuse serve.py's existing `watchfiles` loop (`_watch_ops_files`, which today rebroadcasts a full `state_snapshot`) to trigger incremental re-projection: diff the recompiled state against the doc and apply only the changed fields inside one Yjs transaction, so remote clients see minimal deltas rather than a full replace.\n- Deterministic mapping: two processes projecting the same ops must converge to identical doc content (test: project in two fresh docs, compare state vectors/encoded updates after the same op sequence).\n- Mark projection-origin transactions (Yjs transaction origin) so the write-back bridge can ignore them (idempotence).\n## Done when\nUnit tests: snapshot -> doc -> snapshot round trip is lossless for the live-editable fields; applying one `update` op produces a one-field delta; convergence test passes. Coverage 100% per repo rule.\n## Context\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_10162026_2318.md section 4 (proposed item). Python binding: pycrdt 0.14.9 (y-py is unmaintained)."  # ea14
    fields: {}  # ea14
